# Enforce LF normalization on Windows
#
# NOTE: the `* text=lf` catch-all at the bottom DOES NOTHING. `lf` is not a valid
# value for the `text` attribute — git accepts set / unset / `auto` and treats
# anything else as undefined, falling through to core.autocrlf. Every extension
# that needs LF must therefore be listed EXPLICITLY below; `eol=lf` works because
# it implies text. This gap silently let a Windows tool commit 2276 CRLF lines
# into WORKSPACE/DISCOVERIES.md on 2026-08-05.
#
# Deliberately left in place rather than changed to `* text=auto`, which would
# mark the whole tree for renormalization (user decision, 2026-08-06). Every
# extension listed here was verified LF-clean in the tree at the time it was
# added, so none of these lines rewrites an existing file.

# Code
*.cs eol=lf
*.csproj eol=lf
*.sln eol=lf
*.lua eol=lf
*.py eol=lf
*.ts eol=lf

# Data / config
*.yaml eol=lf
*.yml eol=lf
*.json eol=lf
*.ftl eol=lf
*.in eol=lf

# Docs / prose
*.md eol=lf
*.txt eol=lf
*.html eol=lf

# Scripts — .cmd and .ps1 included deliberately: all are already LF in-tree and
# run correctly that way, so pinning them costs nothing and stops a Windows
# editor from flipping them.
*.sh eol=lf
*.ps1 eol=lf
*.cmd eol=lf

# Inert — see the note at the top. Kept only so its absence isn't read as an
# intentional removal; it provides no normalization.
* text=lf

# Custom for Visual Studio
*.cs     diff=csharp
